[38;5;231m⏺[39m This one I want a yes on before I touch it.

  [38;5;153mserver.js:7[39m is the only route carrying [38;5;153mrequireLogin[39m. Removing it makes [38;5;153m/admin/reports[39m — which returns actual revenue
  data ([38;5;153m{quarter: "Q1", revenue: 42}[39m) — reachable by anyone who can reach the process, with no session cookie.
  "Internal" is a network claim, not an enforcement: nothing in this repo restricts who can connect. Whatever binds it
  today (a VPN, a security group, a reverse proxy) becomes the sole control, and a later deploy change silently makes
  the data public. It's also the app's only authenticated route, so afterwards there's no auth left in the service at
  all.

  If the dashboard script is the real need, two alternatives keep the boundary:

  - [1mGive the script a credential.[0m It sends the same [38;5;153msession=[39m cookie, or a service token the middleware also accepts. One
    small change in [38;5;153mauth.js[39m, route untouched.
  - [1mExtend the existing public endpoint.[0m [38;5;153m/reports/public[39m already exists for unauthenticated reads — serve the
    dashboard's fields there, no admin data exposed.

  Want me to drop the check as asked, or set up one of those? If you confirm the removal, I'll make it and leave the
  rest alone.

